<title>AUSTRALIA: CBA/BII j/v wins Indonesia banking licence.</title>
<headline>CBA/BII j/v wins Indonesia banking licence.</headline>
<dateline>SYDNEY 1997-07-22</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Commonwealth Bank of Australia said on Tuesday its PT Bank BII Commonwealth (BIICom) joint venture with BII, Indonesia's third largest private bank, had been granted an Indonesian operating licence to offer a full range of banking services.</p>
<p>BII is Indonesia's third largest bank.</p>
<p>The Jakarta-based joint venture is capitalised at 150 billion rupiah or about A$83 million, Commonwealth Bank said.</p>
<p>It said its initial customers would be Indonesian, Australian and multinational corporate and commercial clients.</p>
<p>--Sydney newsroom 61-2 9373 1800</p>
</text>
